-- title:
--   Reducedness of the edge chart ring over W(k)/p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Form the ring of Witt vectors $W(k)$ and the ideal $\mathrm{pIdeal}\,p\,W(k)$ generated by the single element $p$, and put $\bar k = W(k)/(p)$. The assertion is that the ring `EdgeFamily.edgeRingCharP p` evaluated at $\bar k$, that is `FormalOmega.chartERing` of $\bar k$ at the parameter $\pi = 0$ and with $q = p$, is reduced: it has no nonzero nilpotent elements. By definition this ring is the localisation of `FormalOmega.edgeQuot` $\bar k\,(0)$ away from the element `FormalOmega.edgeQuot.discr` $\bar k\,(0)\,p$, where `FormalOmega.edgeQuot` $\bar k\,(0)$ is the quotient of the polynomial ring $\bar k[X_0,X_1]$ in two variables by the principal ideal generated by `FormalOmega.edgeRel` $\bar k\,(0)$, which for the parameter value $0$ is the monomial $X_0X_1$. So the conclusion says that the localisation of $\bar k[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1)$ at the relevant discriminant element is reduced.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra input saying that the standard edge chart of the Čerednik–Drinfeld model, taken over the residue field $W(k)/p$ of the Witt vectors of an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, is a reduced ring. It is used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.eq_of_isQuadrupleOf_of_isCartierQuadruple_map_of_forall_algClosed_line_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.eq_of_isQuadrupleOf_of_isCartierQuadruple_map_of_forall_algClosed_line_eq), where data over a reduced base ring are recognised by their geometric points.
